  <p>The Core sequence has now moved from the interacting electron–nuclear problem to fermionic references, periodic states, density-functional reformulation, finite computation, ground-state properties, response, and finally excitations. A real electronic-structure paper can combine several of these layers, but its claims become intelligible only when the physical object, approximation, representation, solution, and probe are kept distinct.</p>

